adjudication.rationale:
In `GroupAdapter#getSubGroupsCount()` the diff changes behavior from always delegating to `getGroupModel().getSubGroupsCount()` to returning `null` when `modelSupplier.get()` returns `null`:
```java
GroupModel model = modelSupplier.get();
return model == null ? null : model.getSubGroupsCount();
```
This introduces a new nullable return path for a “count” method. Any existing callers that assume a non-null count (including common `long` unboxing patterns) can now hit a `NullPointerException` at the call site. The diff itself shows the new `null` return possibility, which is a correctness regression risk.
